ADR-0056 W1 / WI-jijor. `validate_pass_dependencies` had eleven call sites and
all eleven were tests; `validate_pass_name_resolution` had zero anywhere,
under a docstring claiming it ran "at catalog-build time and in CI". The ~73
depends_on conjuncts across 59 passes had never been checked against a run.

Ships the same CNF predicate pointed the other way:
`find_falsified_dependencies(passes, runs)` reports a pass that EMITTED
OUTPUT despite an unsatisfied conjunct, which proves the DECLARATION wrong
rather than the run. It reports and never raises, so unlike the gate INV-hujog
asks for it cannot lose an edge. `validate_pass_dependencies` is untouched.

Output counts nodes_emitted OR edges_emitted -- keying on edges alone is the
instrument fault that inflated a recent cost figure 27x. A pass that ran and
found nothing still SATISFIES a clause naming it: active means active, never
productive.

The reader is wired on the survey path next to the pass-silence summary, one
stderr line, silent when clean, and proven to fire: a Go-only repo at tip
names inheritance-linker and type-hierarchy-linker.

First audit over 893 surveys carrying analysis_runs: 261 (29.2%) carry a
falsified declaration, six distinct (pass, clause) across five passes. Filed
for repair as its own row; ADR-0056's "ten hits means declaration repair is
the blocker" criterion is met.

Also repairs a control that could not fail: TestCatalogStaticConsistency built
the catalog without importing the linker modules, which register by import
side-effect, so in isolation it validated 118 analyzers and ZERO conjuncts.
Now imports them, asserts a named declaration (not just a count), and goes red
under an injected mutation.

